-- computes its weights at runtime, so these are CLASSIC's numbers applied to
-- Forever. That holds structurally, and measured over every position rather
-- than a sample — the two clients' trees carry the same 432 talents across the
-- same 27 trees, each at an identical class/tab/tier/column, with maxRank
-- differing at NONE of them. 35 are RENAMED in place, keeping their position
-- and their spell id: Warrior's Axe / Mace / Sword Specialization all display
-- as "Weaponmaster" and Rogue's Dagger / Mace / Sword as "Hack and Slash",
-- but each is still a separate talent with its own spell — nothing merged.
--
-- THE TALENT EFFECTS DIFFER, and this header said they had 'not been compared'
-- until 2026-09-22, which was true when written and stale by the time anyone
-- read it. Reading SpellEffect for every talent spell shared by both clients:
-- 30 of the 32 renamed talents differ, and 265 of the 383 same-NAMED ones
-- differ too, 147 of them structurally. So the tree these weights were tuned
-- against is not the tree this client runs, and `authoredFor` says Vanilla for
-- that reason -- it is the honest statement and it covers the WHOLE scale.
--
